3
00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:08.215
you've turned me into a giddy girl, I can't help it.

4
00:00:08.215 --> 00:00:09.240
(Hailee laughs)

5
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.280
I wanna thank you for inspiring me

6
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.010
to pick up this collected poem of Emily Dickinson.

7
00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:18.080
I saw season one, by the way, David Gordon Green,

8
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:19.960
the director who directed the premiere

9
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.450
in the first episode is one of my favorite directors.

10
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:23.809
The best.

11
00:00:23.809 --> 00:00:25.390
And I just loved the tone of it.

12
00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:27.350
And now season two, I've been watching that.

13
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:28.313
It's incredible.

14
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.120
You have been a huge fan of Emily Dickinson

15
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:34.670
before the show, is this right?

16
00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:38.800
Yeah, so I came across, Emily's work in school,

17
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.690 line:15%
but I hadn't, I never spent as much time

18
00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:43.350 line:15%
as I have with her because of the show.

19
00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.330 line:15%
And I am equally as thankful to this show

20
00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:48.660
for sort of reintroducing me to her

21
00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.830
and her story, and her poetry, because it is so incredible.

22
00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:55.190
And I have really felt so impacted

23
00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.163
by her work and her words.

24
00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.760
I almost wish I came across it sooner,

25
00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.530
at least to this degree,

26
00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.430
but I guess that's why we have the show now.

27
00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:07.540
And I am so excited about it

28
00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.283
and grateful that we have a season two out,

29
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.750
and very excited for people to see it.

30
00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:18.750
She must be a very emotional person to portray and embody.

31
00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.403
Did that take over and affect?

32
00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.890
Absolutely, one thing about Emily's poetry

33
00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:26.593
that you will find very quickly.

34
00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.683
She talks about everything,

35
00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:33.120
from death

36
00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:36.660
to demons,

37
00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:39.730
and light, nature, trees, butterflies,

38
00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:40.700
and everything in between.

39
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.100
And it is, it is emotional, exactly what you said.

40
00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.120
It's, it takes you to dark, darker places,

41
00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.370
and places you don't necessarily

42
00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.283
want to spend a lot of time in,

43
00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:51.970
but what's so wonderful about this show

44
00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:54.460 line:15%
is it touches on that, and in the same moment,

45
00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.410 line:15%
or in the next moment, you're laughing,

46
00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:58.820 line:15%
and there, it's, there's humor behind it

47
00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:01.220 line:15%
that makes it feel, you know,

48
00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.850
as light as it can dark sometimes,

49
00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.140
it's got really everything in it,

50
00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:07.060
and it's all driven by her poetry.

51
00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:11.530
It's incredibly delightful, yet full of depth.

52
00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:16.263
And I know it won a Peabody Award, which is just.

53
00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:19.493
Thank you.

54
00:02:19.493 --> 00:02:21.580
I know, it's really such an honor.

55
00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:25.040
I mean, to be making a story about a woman

56
00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.933
who spent the majority of her life,

57
00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:31.720
you know, unseen, at least she felt

58
00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:33.870
unseen and misunderstood.

59
00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:36.400
And beyond that, no one even knew her work

60
00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.570
until after she died, and to be making a show

61
00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:43.130
about that and having the opportunity,

62
00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:46.240
in my position, to be an actor that has a platform

63
00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.986
and has a voice, it's made me realize how grateful I am,

64
00:02:48.986 --> 00:02:51.850
and you know, to the Peabody Awards,

65
00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:54.090
so incredibly grateful that they continue

66
00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:56.870
to shine a light on stories that mean something,

67
00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:58.360
and this is a show that is about

68
00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.800
not putting people in a box, and seeing,

69
00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:03.700
and being seen, and being accepted for who you are.

70
00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:06.130
And we can never have enough of those.

71
00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:08.070
And so, I'm incredibly honored that

72
00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:10.340
we were given that reward.

73
00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:11.410
And is it true?
(audience applauding)

74
00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:12.243
I know.

75
00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:14.360
It's so wonderful.

76
00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.950
I had to talk about that.

77
00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:20.950
And is it true, also, that each episode is based on a poem?

78
00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:23.090
Yes, yes, and it's fun.

79
00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:25.510
Oftentimes, I will associate my favorite poem

80
00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:27.390
with my favorite episode,

81
00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:29.760
and it changes all the time, I find.

82
00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.570
But Alena Smith, our writer and creator, is a genius.

83
00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:36.870
And my Emily Dickinson encyclopedia,

84
00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:38.140
as I like to call her.

85
00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:39.650
And knows anything and everything

86
00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:40.500
there is to know about her,

87
00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:43.120
and she has taken what we do know about her life,

88
00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:48.120
and the rest is us interpreting her crazy mind,

89
00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.060
and again, using her poetry,

90
00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.580
and we get the result of a really fun show.

91
00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:56.220
Well, I loved hearing that detail while watching it,

92
00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.140
and knowing that piece of information,

93
00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.191
'cause it's a very clever structure.

94
